# CLI entrypoint

- All user-facing command-line workflows start from **`src/main.py`** (Typer app).
- Prefer:

```bash
uv run python src/main.py <command> [options]
```

- Keep `main.py` thin: create the Typer `app` and **register** commands from `src/cli/`.
- Put each command in its own file under `src/cli/` (one primary command function per file).
- HTTP CLIs live under `src/cli/http/<domain>/` and are mounted as `main.py http <domain> <command>`.
- Command bodies stay thin — call into `pipeline/`, `agents/`, `hc_http/`, or `tools/`.
- Do not add new top-level scripts under `scripts/` for product features (validator/CI scripts already in-repo are fine).
- Do not tell users to run `uv run python src/pipeline/...` or `src/agents/...` directly for normal workflows.

```python
# ✅ main.py — register only
from cli.cognito_login import cognito_login
from cli.http import app as http_app

app = typer.Typer(...)
app.command("cognito-login")(cognito_login)
app.add_typer(http_app, name="http")

# ✅ cli/http/__init__.py — domain subgroups
app.add_typer(fda_app, name="fda")

# ✅ cli/http/fda/search_tradename.py — thin HTTP command
def search_tradename(tradename: str) -> None:
    typer.echo(json.dumps(search_fdalabel_tradename(tradename), indent=2))
```
